---
import DocsLayout from '../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import MermaidDiagram from '../components/MermaidDiagram.astro';
import { runtimeStateDiagram } from '../data/diagrams';
---

<DocsLayout title="Runtime State" sectionLabel="How It Works" activeSlug="runtime">

  <div class="panel-intro">
    <h2>Runtime State</h2>
    <p>Every project using VibeCrew gets a <code>.vibecrew/</code> folder that stores all runtime state: project configuration, foundation progress, feature backlog, session logs, Vibe Scores, architecture diagrams, and cross-session handoffs. This folder is the system's memory &mdash; it persists between sessions and lets agents pick up exactly where the last one left off.</p>
    <div class="key-points">
      <div class="key-point">
        <span class="key-icon purple">&#9632;</span>
        <div>
          <strong>What it is</strong>
          <p>A directory of JSON files and sub-folders created by <code>/setup</code>. Core files: <code>config.json</code> (preferences), <code>state.json</code> (current phase), <code>backlog.json</code> (feature specs), <code>gamification.json</code> (progression). Sub-directories hold sessions, scores, signals, locks, and architecture diagrams.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="key-point">
        <span class="key-icon green">&#10003;</span>
        <div>
          <strong>What problem it solves</strong>
          <p>AI sessions are stateless &mdash; each new conversation starts from scratch. The <code>.vibecrew/</code> folder gives the system persistent memory: which features are done, what phase you're in, your quality trends, and even architectural diagrams that agents reference instead of re-deriving structure from code.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h4 class="agent-table-heading">Core State Files</h4>
  <p class="cmd-group-desc">JSON files that store project configuration and progress.</p>
  <div class="agent-table-wrap">
    <table class="agent-table">
      <thead><tr><th>File</th><th>Read By</th><th>What It Stores</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><code>config.json</code></td>
          <td>All agents, hooks, status bar</td>
          <td>Terminal preferences, notification settings, user profile (role, verbosity, autonomy, etc.), cost thresholds, and MCP server toggles.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>state.json</code></td>
          <td>All agents, hooks, status bar</td>
          <td>Foundation completion status, active feature name, current phase, plan revision count, feature history, and last session timestamp.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>backlog.json</code></td>
          <td>Orchestrator, Builder, dashboard</td>
          <td>Feature specifications with Kanban columns (Ideas &rarr; Planned &rarr; In Progress &rarr; Testing &rarr; Review &rarr; Done), priority, complexity (trivial/standard/complex), milestones, and acceptance criteria.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>gamification.json</code></td>
          <td>Performance Coach, dashboard</td>
          <td>XP, level, earned badges, skill tree progress, active streaks, and challenge completions. Opt-in via <code>/profile</code>.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h4 class="agent-table-heading">Runtime Directories</h4>
  <p class="cmd-group-desc">Sub-directories that store session data and inter-agent communication.</p>
  <div class="agent-table-wrap">
    <table class="agent-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Directory</th><th>What It Stores</th><th>Who Uses It</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><code>architecture/</code></td>
          <td>5 Mermaid <code>.mmd</code> files: system topology, ER schema, state flows, API sequences, and component tree.</td>
          <td>Builder (reads for context), Doc Generator (freshness check), injected once per session.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>sessions/</code></td>
          <td>JSON logs for each session: start/end time, features worked on, Vibe Score, token usage, cost.</td>
          <td>Performance Coach (trend analysis), dashboard (stats/trends tabs).</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>scores/</code></td>
          <td>Detailed Vibe Score breakdowns: each deduction and bonus with reasons.</td>
          <td>Performance Coach, dashboard (trends tab), status bar (current score).</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>signals/</code></td>
          <td>Inter-agent signal files for communication between worktree agents and the main session.</td>
          <td>Agents (write signals), hooks (validate schema before write).</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>locks/</code></td>
          <td>Advisory lock files that prevent concurrent modifications to shared state.</td>
          <td>Scripts (acquire/release), error recovery (clear stale locks).</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>handoffs/</code></td>
          <td>Structured context transfer documents created by <code>/handoff</code> for cross-session continuity.</td>
          <td>Session Startup (detects and loads), agents (reads for context).</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>analysis/</code></td>
          <td>4 persistent markdown files from <code>/onboard</code>: <code>stack.md</code> (language, framework, deps), <code>architecture.md</code> (dirs, patterns, API style), <code>conventions.md</code> (formatting, naming, test patterns), <code>gaps.md</code> (coverage, untested modules, TODOs). Refreshable via <code>/onboard --refresh</code>.</td>
          <td>Builder (Plan phase injection), compact-reinject (post-compaction context), Session Startup (staleness check).</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>releases/</code></td>
          <td>Release notes data (JSON) with version history and feature summaries.</td>
          <td>Doc Generator (<code>/release</code>), dashboard releases tab.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>workflows/</code></td>
          <td>Reusable workflow templates extracted from high-scoring sessions via <code>/replay</code>.</td>
          <td>Orchestrator (loads templates for replay).</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>expertise/</code></td>
          <td>Persistent agent expertise records &mdash; learned patterns and session learnings (JSON).</td>
          <td>Performance Coach (writes), Builder and Code Reviewer (read for adaptive behavior).</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>memory/</code></td>
          <td>Per-agent persistent memory &mdash; operational knowledge accumulated across sessions (JSONL). Organized as <code>memory/&lt;agent&gt;/&lt;domain&gt;.jsonl</code> with TTL-based auto-pruning.</td>
          <td>Builder (API patterns, conventions), Verifier (flaky tests), Stack Scout (library gotchas), Code Reviewer (recurring issues).</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>agent-overrides/</code></td>
          <td>Per-project agent customization files (<code>&lt;agent&gt;.md</code>). Sections with matching headings replace the base agent&rsquo;s sections; new headings are appended. Frontmatter (model, tools, isolation) is always preserved from the base agent. Survives plugin updates.</td>
          <td>All agents (loaded via <code>load-agent-with-overrides.sh</code> at agent start).</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <MermaidDiagram chart={runtimeStateDiagram} caption="Runtime state files and who reads/writes them" />

</DocsLayout>
